{'symbol': 'PCG', 'date': '2022-10-04 13:35:00', 'title': 'CLIMATE CREDIT FROM STATE PROGRAM WILL LOWER BILLS THIS MONTH', 'text': "OAKLAND, CALIF.--(BUSINESS WIRE)--MORE THAN 5 MILLION PACIFIC GAS AND ELECTRIC COMPANY (PG&E) ELECTRIC CUSTOMERS WILL AUTOMATICALLY RECEIVE THE CALIFORNIA CLIMATE CREDIT ON THEIR ENERGY BILL THIS MONTH. THE CREDIT WAS CREATED BY THE CALIFORNIA PUBLIC UTILITIES COMMISSION (CPUC) AS PART OF THE STATE'S EFFORTS TO FIGHT CLIMATE CHANGE. PG&E IS PLEASED TO ADMINISTER THE CREDIT IN A TIMELY MANNER TO HELP REDUCE CUSTOMER ENERGY BILLS THIS MONTH. IN ADDITION TO RESIDENTIAL CUSTOMERS, ELIGIBLE"}